# Changelog - xcesp-l2tpv3d

## 0.2.0

- **ControlMessage wire codec** (`xcesp_l2tpv3d/messages.py`) — the 12-byte
  L2TPv3 control-message header per RFC 3931 §4.1.1: T/L/S flag bits,
  4 reserved bits (validated zero on decode), 4-bit Version (=3),
  Length (16-bit), Control Connection ID (32-bit), Ns (16-bit), Nr
  (16-bit).  Encode + decode + ZLB detection.  Rejects data messages
  (T=0), missing L/S bits, non-zero reserved bits, wrong version,
  length/buffer mismatch, out-of-range CCID/Ns/Nr.
- **Sequence-number arithmetic** (`seq_delta`, `seq_advance`) — wrap-
  safe 16-bit comparison per RFC 3931 §5.8 (values in [0, 32767] mean
  "ahead", values in [-32768, -1] mean "behind"; the 0x8000 boundary
  is exactly `-0x8000` per L2TP half-window semantics).
- **Peer state machine** (`xcesp_l2tpv3d/transport.py`) — per-remote
  reliable delivery.  Time-agnostic: caller passes a monotonic `now`
  on every call, so retransmit behaviour is deterministically
  testable against a mocked clock.  Owns:
    * `_ns_send` / `_nr_expect` counters (16-bit, wrap-safe).
    * Send queue of unacked messages, cleared as peer's Nr advances.
    * Reorder buffer bounded by `receive_window`.
    * Retransmit timer with RFC 3931 §5.8 exponential back-off:
      1s → 2s → 4s → 8s → 16s (capped, `RETRANSMIT_MAX_INTERVAL`).
    * Dead-peer detection when `max_retries` exceeded.
    * ZLB (Zero-Length Body) ack-only messages that don't consume Ns
      and aren't themselves acked.
    * Nr-refresh on retransmit (so the resent copy carries our latest
      acknowledgement, not the stale Nr from first transmission).
- **Transport abstraction** (`Transport` ABC + `UdpTransport` for
  asyncio production + `LoopbackTransport` for tests).  Loopback
  variant uses a shared in-memory fabric dict; supports `drop_next`
  for injecting packet loss in tests.
- **Unit tests** — 48 new (+69 from 0.1.0 = 117 total, 0.20s green):
    * ControlMessage: ZLB / with-AVP round-trip, header flag byte
      constant, version, length-match, plus 8 malformed-input rejects.
    * seq_delta / seq_advance: zero, positive/negative no-wrap,
      positive/negative across wrap, half-window boundary, wrap on advance.
    * Peer.send: Ns assignment + advance, remote CCID stamping,
      current Nr piggyback, empty-AVPs rejection, retransmit queueing.
    * Peer.receive: in-order deliver, duplicate re-ack, out-of-order
      within window (reorder queue drains when hole fills), outside
      window drop, ZLB no-op, wrong-CCID drop.
    * Ack consumption: piggybacked Nr and peer-ZLB both flush queue.
    * Retransmit: RTO trigger, exponential back-off progression, cap
      at 16s, dead-peer after max_retries, dead sticks, Nr refresh.
    * LoopbackTransport: two-peer HELLO exchange + ack; lossy-drop
      case where first datagram is dropped and retransmit recovers.
- **pytest-asyncio** added as an optional test dep (auto-mode in
  `pyproject.toml` so async tests need no decorator).

## 0.1.0

- **First release of XCESP's L2TPv3 (RFC 3931) dynamic-mode
  control-plane daemon.**  This is the first free-software Linux
  implementation of the L2TPv3 control channel — OpenL2TP is
  L2TPv2-only, go-l2tp's ql2tpd is static+keepalive between two
  ql2tpd instances (not RFC 3931 negotiation), and prol2tp is
  proprietary.
- **Scope of 0.1.0** — subproject skeleton + AVP codec + unit
  tests only.  No wire I/O.  Sets up the module layout the
  0.2.x-0.9.x releases will fill in per the roadmap plan file.
- **AVP codec** (`xcesp_l2tpv3d/avp.py`) — encode/decode of the RFC
  3931 §5.2 AVP header (M/H bits, reserved, 10-bit length, vendor
  ID, attribute type) plus per-type value serialisation for the
  mandatory AVP set required by SCCRQ/SCCRP/SCCCN/ICRQ/ICRP/ICCN
  message building in future releases: Message Type (0), Result
  Code (1), Random Vector (36), Message Digest (59), Router ID
  (60), Assigned Control Connection ID (61), Pseudowire
  Capabilities List (62), Local Session ID (63), Remote Session
  ID (64), Assigned Cookie (65), Remote End ID (66), Pseudowire
  Type (68), L2-Specific Sublayer (69), Data Sequencing (70),
  Circuit Status (71), Preferred Language (72), Tx Connect Speed
  (74), Rx Connect Speed (75).
- **Hidden-AVP path** (RFC 3931 §4.3) — MD5-keystream encryption
  of Attribute Value using a shared secret + Random Vector AVP;
  round-trips cleanly with a shared-secret fixture.
- **Unit tests** (`test/test_avp.py`) — round-trip every
  implemented AVP type, boundary lengths (empty value, 1-byte,
  256-byte, max 1017-byte), malformed input rejection (short
  header, over-long length, unknown vendor+type).  Runs via
  `make test`.
